    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Wood and Timber Dye Woods Brazil Wood used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 340"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "SAPAN-WOOD: a dye-wood obtained in Malabar, and the islands of the Eastern seas, from the Cesalpinia sappan, C. coriaria, and pulcherrima. A decoction of the wood is used by calico-printers for red dyes."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
